==================================================================================================================
L73 -- CAN THE LEAD'S INTEGRABLE-CLOCK ACTION BE A COMPLETE THEORY, OR ONLY COMPLETE BELOW A GALAXY?
==================================================================================================================
The excess-spent-once theorem (L55/L61) is branch-independent.  L66 showed the lead escapes a DIFFERENT
theorem (the deep-MOND lapse kill) by keeping MOND inside the clock.  This lane asks whether keeping MOND
inside the clock also changes the TRANSMISSION FACTOR that excess-spent-once turns on -- or whether the
cold component still reaches baryons through the single metric with eta=1, binding the theorem anyway.
a0 footings: canonical 9.3619e-11 / alt 1.1279e-10 m/s^2 (both carried).  kappa=1/2 FITTED.

