==================================================================================================================
PART B -- THE TRANSMISSION CHANNEL IN THE LEAD'S ACTION.  Is the MOND-producing channel the same as
==================================================================================================================
                    the cold-matter transmission channel, and does the difference change eta?

Read from IC4_ACTION.md's own equations (offline; nothing imported).  The full action is

   S4 = INT sqrt(-g) { (m/2)[ R4 - 2Lambda + 4KW - 6W^2 + 2(1-u^2) a.a - 2 a0^2 U(u^2)
                              + (Q^2/a0^2)(J + Rhat F) ] + kappa X }  +  S_m[g,psi].

Two facts are stated verbatim in the action file and fix the channels:
  (1) 'The independently diffeomorphism-invariant S_m[g,psi] is unchanged.  Its own on-shell Ward
      identity remains grad_mu T^{mu nu}=0.  No extra force on ordinary matter is inserted.'
  (2) The MOND scale a0 enters the CLOCK's own acceleration invariant  2(1-u^2)a_mu a^mu - 2 a0^2 U,
      with a_mu = D_mu ln N and N=(2X)^{-1/2} a functional of the clock T.  There is NO separate MOND
      scalar phi and NO AeST coupling 2(2-K_B) a^mu d_mu phi  (this is exactly the L66 escape).

B.1  The cold-matter transmission channel.  A pressureless component -- whatever supplies it -- enters
     the field equations through its stress T^{mu nu}, which sources the SAME physical metric g via the
     Einstein-Hilbert term (m/2)R4.  Baryons are minimally coupled to that SAME g (fact 1).  So a cold
     component's Newtonian pull reaches a baryon by ORDINARY GRAVITY IN g -- the identical channel at
     recombination and in a galaxy, because it is ONE metric at BOTH epochs.  The transmission factor is
     therefore eta = 1 (pure gravity) at both, with no scale- or environment-dependence available.
      channel(cold->baryon) = minimal gravitational coupling to the single metric g  ==>  eta_galaxy = eta_recomb = 1
  [PASS] B1  the cold-matter transmission channel is minimal coupling to the SINGLE metric g, identical at recombination and in galaxies (single-metric + minimal matter coupling, from S_m[g,psi], no extra force)   (eta is epoch-independent: there is no second metric or non-minimal coupling to make it differ)

B.2  The MOND-production channel.  The a0 scale rides the clock's acceleration invariant, NOT a separate
     scalar's kernel.  This IS a different channel from B.1's -- which is precisely why the lead escapes
     the L60/L69 lapse-channel kill (L66 LEAD-6).  The question this lane must answer is whether that
     difference reaches the transmission factor eta.
      channel(MOND) = clock acceleration invariant 2(1-u^2)a.a - 2a0^2 U(u^2)  =/=  channel(cold->baryon)
  [PASS] B2  the MOND-producing channel and the cold-matter transmission channel are DIFFERENT channels in the lead's action (MOND in the clock; cold matter through g)   (confirmed from the action; the crux is whether that difference changes eta)

B.3  THE CRUX.  Excess-spent-once needs eta SMALLER in galaxies than at recombination (A2: <=0.58 vs
     1.00).  eta is a property of the cold-matter -> baryon channel ALONE (B.1).  Producing MOND in a
     separate clock channel (B.2) changes A_K (the anomaly the kernel adds); it leaves the cold-matter
     channel -- minimal coupling to the single metric g -- UNTOUCHED.  So the different MOND channel
     does NOT change eta.  To make eta<1 in galaxies the lead would need to break B.1's channel itself:
     a SECOND metric for the cold component (the action is explicitly single-metric: 'the barred metric
     is a change of variables on the clock slices, NOT a second metric for matter or light'), or a
     non-minimal coupling (fact 1 forbids it: no extra force on ordinary matter).  Neither exists here,
     and the only environmental/range escapes are A3's four wrong orderings.
      lever 'second metric for the cold component': not available / wrong ordering
      lever 'non-minimal (disformal/conformal) matter coupling': not available / wrong ordering
      lever 'a range / graviton mass (Yukawa)': not available / wrong ordering
      lever 'monotone environmental screening (rho / g / Phi)': not available / wrong ordering
  [PASS] B3  [THE CRUX]  keeping MOND inside the clock does NOT change the transmission factor eta: eta is set by the cold-matter->baryon channel (single metric, minimal coupling), which the clock leaves untouched -- so hypothesis (c) BINDS and no escape channel exists   (no single-metric, minimally-coupled lever suppresses the cold pull in galaxies)

